    "final_answer": "I have found the answer. Wolfram Alpha has confirmed the character information clearly in the results page.\n\n## Answer\n\nThe character in Unicode range 9632 to 9650 that represents a hollow parallelogram is:\n\n**Unicode 9649 (U+25B1) — WHITE PARALLELOGRAM**\n\n**Symbol:** ▱\n\n### Verification from Wolfram Alpha:\n- **Name (名称):** white parallelogram (the \"hollow\" version, as opposed to the filled black parallelogram at 9648)\n- **Unicode:** U+25B1 (decimal: 9649)\n- **HTML:** `&#x25B1;` or `&#9649;`\n- **Wolfram Language:** `\\:25b1`\n\nThe character ▱ is rendered as an outlined (hollow) parallelogram shape. It is part of the Geometric Shapes block (U+25A0–U+25FF), which contains various squares, rectangles, parallelograms, and triangles. Its filled counterpart, the BLACK PARALLELOGRAM ▰, is at Unicode 9648 (U+25B0).",
